# Bare-identifier assign of a Box[T] still requires explicit `!`.
#
# Per the CoW-by-default rule (2026-05-12), bare assign of non-Copy
# user structs / enums / collections / strings now flows through the
# IR-lowering's Phase D4 CoW machinery — `b = a` borrows `a` and CoW-
# severs on mutation. Box[T] is the exception: it's a single-owner
# heap allocation whose value semantics ARE move semantics, so the
# safety pass still rejects bare assignment.
void main():
    Box[int] a = Box(42)
    Box[int] b = a
    print(b)
